# Cursor Rules — Pare (NFL head-to-head comparison app)

## Standing engineering rules (ALWAYS apply — do not re-read CLAUDE.md for these)
- Stack: Next.js 15 + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind v3. Dev server on port 4000.
- DARK MODE ONLY. Mobile-first — design at ~390px; this web app is the base for an iOS app.
- TypeScript strict, no `any`; typed props/interfaces. Hooks hold logic; components render.
- Tailwind utility classes + design tokens. No ad-hoc inline styles.
- SURGICAL over rebuild: small, atomic, scoped to exactly what's asked. Don't refactor
  unrelated code.
- Do NOT change the data layer, the ranking / display-mode / bar-calculation math, or hook
  signatures unless the task explicitly says so. Preserve the theScore inward-bar logic —
  it's the heart of the app.
- No duplicate global state — team selection lives at ComparePage level, passed via props.
- Data source: schedule + stats come from ESPN (see DATA_SOURCES.md). Team yards use NET
  (netPassingYards / netTotalYards) so offense matches defense-allowed. Defense yards/3rd-down
  are opponent-aggregated from box scores. Cache fetches (~6h) and ALWAYS keep a fallback so
  the app never blanks.

## Verification (token-thrifty — important)
- Do NOT open a browser, drive it, or take screenshots to self-verify. Kobe checks the UI.
- Verify with cheap checks ONLY: curl + jq, row counts, internal-consistency assertions,
  and `npm run lint`. Print the numbers, don't screenshot.

## When to read the big docs (don't by default)
- CLAUDE.md: read only for architecture-level or cross-cutting work.
- DATA_SOURCES.md: read only when wiring or changing data endpoints.
- For a scoped, surgical change, skip both — these standing rules cover it.
- Do NOT print "Rule Summary / Ambiguities / Confirmation" blocks unless asked.

## Docs ritual (keep, but lightweight)
- Conventional Commits: feat: / fix: / docs: / chore:.
- Non-trivial change → append a short Dev Note at docs/devnotes/YYYY-MM-DD-<task>.md
  (rationale only; link CLAUDE.md, don't duplicate it) + a CHANGELOG [Unreleased] bullet
  linking it. Skip the note for tiny one-line fixes.
- Create an ADR (docs/adr/) only for a genuine architectural decision.
- CLAUDE.md stays the source of truth for deep rules; promote a rule there only when it's reusable.
